---
import { legalDocuments } from "../../../site.config.mjs";
import { overLitConfig } from "../../config/site";

const appName = overLitConfig.name;
const appPageUrl = new URL(overLitConfig.homeHref, overLitConfig.origin).toString();
const supportPageUrl = new URL(overLitConfig.supportHref, overLitConfig.origin).toString();
const privacyPolicyUrl = new URL(overLitConfig.privacyHref, overLitConfig.origin).toString();
const appAdsTxtUrl = new URL("/app-ads.txt", overLitConfig.origin).toString();
const googlePrivacyHref = "https://policies.google.com/privacy";
const googleAdsTechnologiesHref = "https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads";
const applePrivacyHref = "https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/";
const appleAppStoreTermsHref = "https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/";
const metaPrivacyHref = "https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/";
const tiktokPrivacyHref = "https://www.tiktok.com/legal/page/eea/privacy-policy/en";
---

<h1>{appName} Privacy Policy</h1>

<p>
  <strong>Effective Date:</strong> {legalDocuments.overLitPrivacy.effectiveDate}<br />
  <strong>Version:</strong> {legalDocuments.overLitPrivacy.version}
</p>

<p>
  This Privacy Policy explains how {appName} handles information when you use the iPhone app,
  visit the OverLit pages on this website, contact support, or interact with ads shown in or for
  {appName}.
</p>

<p>
  {appName} is provided by Aleksander Jałtuszyk (&quot;Developer&quot;, &quot;we&quot;, &quot;us&quot;,
  or &quot;our&quot;). Country: Poland. Contact: <code>{overLitConfig.supportEmail}</code>.
  Support page: <a href={supportPageUrl}>{supportPageUrl}</a>.
</p>

<p>
  This policy covers the {appName} app and the OverLit pages on
  <code>alekjaltuszyk.xyz</code>, including:
</p>

<ul>
  <li><a href={appPageUrl}>{appPageUrl}</a></li>
  <li><a href={supportPageUrl}>{supportPageUrl}</a></li>
  <li><a href={privacyPolicyUrl}>{privacyPolicyUrl}</a></li>
</ul>

<h2>1. Summary</h2>

<ul>
  <li>{appName} is a short-session iPhone arcade/reflex game.</li>
  <li>The app does not require an account, custom backend, chat, social feed, multiplayer, or cloud sync.</li>
  <li>Gameplay settings, preferences, and high scores may be stored locally on your device.</li>
  <li>
    The app does not ask for account registration, passwords, payment card details, phone numbers,
    mailing addresses, precise GPS location, contacts, camera access, photo library access, or age.
  </li>
  <li>
    The app uses the Google Mobile Ads SDK for AdMob rewarded ads and interstitial ads.
  </li>
  <li>
    The app uses Google User Messaging Platform / AdMob privacy messages for applicable
    European regulations and U.S. state privacy regulations, and may show an AdMob IDFA
    explainer before Apple&apos;s App Tracking Transparency prompt.
  </li>
  <li>
    Google/AdMob may collect or process advertising, device, product interaction, coarse location,
    diagnostic, crash, and performance data as described below and in Google&apos;s own policies.
  </li>
  <li>
    If you allow tracking through Apple App Tracking Transparency and your regional consent choices
    permit it, Google/AdMob and advertising partners may use identifiers such as the IDFA for
    personalized ads, ad measurement, fraud prevention, and related advertising purposes.
  </li>
  <li>
    If you deny tracking, decline consent, or opt out where applicable, ads may still appear without
    IDFA-based or personalized tracking where required.
  </li>
  <li>
    The app may show local developer house ads for PlanKept. Voice of Self is not currently an
    active OverLit ad or promotion. These local house ad panels are not third-party ad network
    requests.
  </li>
  <li>
    We may advertise {appName} on external services such as Instagram, Meta, TikTok, Apple Search
    Ads, Google, or similar platforms. We do not currently install Meta Pixel, TikTok Pixel, Meta
    SDK, TikTok SDK, website/app activity retargeting code, or customer-list uploads for {appName}.
  </li>
  <li>Apple and the App Store may process platform, purchase, device, and privacy data under Apple&apos;s policies.</li>
  <li>We receive support email data only if you choose to contact support.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Data Stored Locally On Your Device</h2>

<p>
  {appName} gameplay is local. The app may store local gameplay/settings data on your device so the
  game can work normally and remember your choices.
</p>

<ul>
  <li>settings and app appearance preferences</li>
  <li>high scores, stats, play progress, mode state, and theme unlocks</li>
  <li>onboarding and legal acceptance state</li>
  <li>play counters and ad counters used to decide when ads or unlock opportunities appear</li>
</ul>

<p>
  This local app data is intended to stay on your device unless you separately choose to send
  information to support, or unless Apple, Google/AdMob, or another platform provider collects or
  processes data through their own platform or advertising services. Deleting the app may remove
  local app data from the device, subject to normal iOS backup, restore, and device behavior.
</p>

<p>
  {appName} does not provide public user-generated content, in-app chat, a social feed, multiplayer,
  or an account system.
</p>

<h2>3. Information We Do Not Ask For</h2>

<p>
  Some template privacy policies include broad categories that do not match {appName}. In the
  current app, we do not ask you to create an account, choose a password, provide a phone number,
  mailing address, billing address, payment card, job title, age, contact list, camera photo, photo
  library item, or precise GPS location.
</p>

<p>
  If you voluntarily include any of that information in a support email, we may receive it as part
  of your message, but the app does not require it.
</p>

<h2>4. Advertising And AdMob</h2>

<p>
  {appName} integrates Google AdMob through the Google Mobile Ads SDK. Release builds use production
  AdMob ad unit IDs. Debug or development builds may use Google demo or test ad IDs.
</p>

<p>
  The app also includes Google User Messaging Platform / AdMob privacy messaging for applicable
  European regulations and U.S. state privacy regulations, an AdMob IDFA explainer, Apple App
  Tracking Transparency, and SKAdNetwork attribution support for privacy-preserving app advertising
  measurement.
</p>

<p>The app currently uses AdMob for:</p>

<ul>
  <li>rewarded ads that let players unlock cosmetic themes</li>
  <li>interstitial ads after natural menu breaks, based on local play-session counters</li>
</ul>

<p>
  Because {appName} is not age-gated and is intended to remain suitable for its App Store age
  rating, the app configures Google Mobile Ads requests with teen treatment and a maximum ad
  content rating no higher than Teen.
</p>

<p>
  Google&apos;s Mobile Ads SDK may collect, receive, or process information such as:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>IP address, which may be used to estimate coarse or general location</li>
  <li>
    device identifiers, including the IDFA when available and allowed, app/developer-bounded
    identifiers, or other advertising identifiers where permitted
  </li>
  <li>advertising data, such as ads shown, impressions, interactions, rewarded ad completion, and related ad events</li>
  <li>product interaction or usage data, such as app launches, taps, video ad views, and other ad-performance events</li>
  <li>
    attribution-related information, including SKAdNetwork-related signals or postbacks handled by
    Apple, Google/AdMob, or advertising partners
  </li>
  <li>crash data and diagnostic logs</li>
  <li>performance data, such as app launch time, hang rate, energy usage, and SDK performance</li>
</ul>

<p>That data may be used for purposes such as:</p>

<ul>
  <li>showing third-party ads in the app</li>
  <li>measuring ad performance and rewarded ad completion</li>
  <li>preventing fraud, abuse, and invalid traffic</li>
  <li>frequency capping, reporting, and campaign measurement</li>
  <li>personalizing ads where you have allowed tracking and any legally required consent permits it</li>
  <li>supporting SKAdNetwork and other privacy-preserving attribution flows</li>
  <li>analytics and performance improvement for the Google Mobile Ads SDK</li>
  <li>diagnostics, reliability, and SDK security</li>
  <li>supporting privacy and consent choices where legally required</li>
</ul>

<p>
  Google and its partners process this information under their own policies. You can read more in
  the <a href={googlePrivacyHref}>Google Privacy Policy</a> and
  <a href={googleAdsTechnologiesHref}>Google&apos;s advertising technologies information</a>.
</p>

<p>
  To support authorized app advertising inventory, this site publishes an
  <a href={appAdsTxtUrl}>app-ads.txt file</a> at <code>{appAdsTxtUrl}</code>. It includes the
  Google publisher record:
</p>

<pre><code>google.com, pub-6606108754134100, DIRECT, f08c47fec0942fa0</code></pre>

<h2>5. Local Developer House Ads</h2>

<p>
  {appName} may show a local developer house ad in the app context, including when AdMob cannot
  load an ad. The current local developer house ads are for PlanKept. Voice of Self is not
  currently an active OverLit ad or promotion.
</p>

<p>
  A house ad is a local in-app panel that promotes the Developer&apos;s own app, app page, App Store
  page, or related app destination.
</p>

<p>
  Showing a local developer house ad does not by itself send data to a third-party ad network. If
  you tap a house ad and leave the app, the destination website, App Store, browser, or device
  platform may process that visit under its own policies.
</p>

<h2>6. External Marketing And Promotion</h2>

<p>
  We may promote {appName} through paid or organic ads on external services such as Instagram,
  Meta, TikTok, Apple Search Ads, Google, or similar advertising platforms.
</p>

<p>
  If you view, click, share, comment on, save, or otherwise interact with an OverLit ad on one of
  those services, that service may process information about the interaction under its own terms,
  privacy policy, and ad settings. For example, Meta/Instagram activity is governed by
  <a href={metaPrivacyHref}>Meta&apos;s Privacy Policy</a>, and TikTok activity is governed by
  <a href={tiktokPrivacyHref}>TikTok&apos;s Privacy Policy</a>.
</p>

<p>
  We do not currently install Meta Pixel, TikTok Pixel, Meta SDK, TikTok SDK, Conversion API,
  app-event SDKs, or similar external marketing trackers in {appName} or on the OverLit website
  pages. We also do not currently upload support emails, contact lists, or customer files to ad
  platforms for OverLit retargeting. If we add those practices later, this policy and the relevant
  platform disclosures should be updated first.
</p>

<h2>7. Privacy Choices And Consent</h2>

<p>
  {appName} may use Google&apos;s User Messaging Platform or AdMob privacy messaging where required.
  Users in applicable regions may see privacy or consent choices for ads, including European
  regulations messages and U.S. state privacy regulation messages. When AdMob reports that privacy
  options are required, {appName} may also make ad privacy options available from the app settings.
</p>

<p>
  On iOS, {appName} may show an AdMob IDFA explainer before Apple&apos;s App Tracking Transparency
  prompt. If you allow tracking and your regional consent choices permit it, Google/AdMob and its
  advertising partners may access or use identifiers such as Apple&apos;s Identifier for Advertisers
  (IDFA) for personalized ads, ad measurement, fraud prevention, frequency capping, and related
  advertising purposes.
</p>

<p>
  If you deny tracking in Apple&apos;s App Tracking Transparency prompt, decline consent, opt out, or
  use device settings that restrict advertising identifiers, ads may still appear without IDFA-based
  or personalized tracking where required. Those ads may be non-personalized, contextual, limited,
  or otherwise served according to Google/AdMob, Apple, and applicable law. If AdMob cannot load,
  {appName} may show a local PlanKept developer house ad instead.
</p>

<p>
  You can manage choices through Google/AdMob consent and privacy flows shown in the app where
  available, and through iOS privacy settings such as App Tracking Transparency, advertising
  identifier controls, and Apple personalized advertising settings where available.
</p>

<h2>8. App Store Privacy Disclosures</h2>

<p>
  Apple&apos;s App Privacy labels use Apple-defined categories and may require disclosures that are
  broader or more conservative than a plain-language policy. The current {appName} App Store privacy
  disclosures are intended to reflect the AdMob setup described above.
</p>

<ul>
  <li>
    Coarse Location, Device Identifiers, Product Interaction or Usage Data, and Advertising Data may
    be disclosed for Third-Party Advertising and Analytics. They may be linked to the user and may
    be used for tracking where Apple&apos;s definitions and the SDK behavior require that disclosure.
  </li>
  <li>
    The app includes Apple App Tracking Transparency because IDFA-based advertising uses may be
    available when you authorize tracking. If tracking is denied, IDFA-based tracking should not be
    used for personalized ads, but non-personalized ads and privacy-preserving measurement may still
    occur where allowed.
  </li>
  <li>
    The app supports SKAdNetwork attribution for ads. SKAdNetwork is an Apple attribution framework
    intended to help measure ad-driven installs or conversions while limiting user- or
    device-specific data in Apple postbacks.
  </li>
  <li>
    Crash Data may be disclosed for Diagnostics and, where applicable, Analytics. It is generally
    not treated as linked to the user by the Developer or used for tracking unless the relevant SDK
    or platform manifest requires otherwise.
  </li>
  <li>
    Performance Data may be disclosed for App Functionality, Analytics, and Third-Party Advertising.
    Because SDK manifests and platform rules can be conservative, it may be disclosed as linked to
    the user and used for tracking where required.
  </li>
</ul>

<p>
  Apple and App Store services are governed by Apple&apos;s own policies, including
  <a href={applePrivacyHref}>Apple&apos;s Privacy Policy</a> and the
  <a href={appleAppStoreTermsHref}>Apple standard terms for apps</a>.
</p>

<h2>9. Support Emails</h2>

<p>
  If you email support, we process your email address, message content, and any details you choose
  to include so we can understand the request and reply. The app itself does not require you to send
  a support email.
</p>

<p>
  Support email: <code>{overLitConfig.supportEmail}</code>. Support page:
  <a href={supportPageUrl}>{supportPageUrl}</a>.
</p>

<p>
  We do not currently use support emails for marketing newsletters, customer-list uploads, or
  retargeting audiences for {appName}. If you want us to delete or correct support information you
  sent, contact us from the same email address when possible so we can verify the request.
</p>

<h2>10. Website Pages, Cookies, And Local Storage</h2>

<p>
  The OverLit pages on <code>alekjaltuszyk.xyz</code> are mostly static and informational. They
  provide the app page, support instructions, this privacy policy, and the public
  <code>app-ads.txt</code> file. We do not currently add a website analytics service or advertising
  cookies to the OverLit pages, so this policy does not add a cookie banner for those pages.
</p>

<p>
  Website hosting and delivery systems may still process ordinary technical information, such as IP
  address, browser type, requested URL, request time, and similar security or server metadata needed
  to deliver the site.
</p>

<p>
  The app uses local on-device storage for gameplay, settings, unlocks, counters, and legal
  acceptance state. Google/AdMob and Apple may use identifiers, SDK storage, consent signals, or
  similar mobile technologies as part of advertising, privacy choices, app distribution, fraud
  prevention, and measurement. External websites or ad platforms you visit from an ad or link may
  use their own cookies, pixels, local storage, sessions, or similar technologies under their own
  policies.
</p>

<h2>11. Third-Party Services And Sharing</h2>

<p>Depending on how you use {appName}, third parties may process information under their own terms:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Google/AdMob and the Google Mobile Ads SDK for in-app advertising and related measurement</li>
  <li>Apple, iOS, and the App Store for platform, device, privacy, download, purchase, and crash/diagnostic services</li>
  <li>Meta/Instagram, TikTok, Apple Search Ads, Google, or similar platforms if you interact with ads for {appName} outside the app</li>
  <li>email providers if you choose to contact support</li>
  <li>website hosting and delivery providers for the public OverLit pages</li>
</ul>

<p>
  We do not control those third parties&apos; privacy practices. Their policies explain how they handle
  information they collect or receive.
</p>

<p>
  We may share or disclose information when reasonably necessary to operate the app, show and
  measure ads, provide support, maintain security, prevent fraud or abuse, comply with law, respond
  to valid legal requests, protect rights and safety, or transfer relevant records in connection
  with a merger, acquisition, reorganization, asset sale, or similar business transfer.
</p>

<p>
  We do not sell support email lists or account lists to data brokers. Some privacy laws define
  certain personalized advertising, ad SDK disclosures, or cross-context ad uses as a &quot;sale,&quot;
  &quot;sharing,&quot; or &quot;targeted advertising.&quot; Where those laws apply, {appName} uses
  AdMob privacy messages and available privacy choices to support opt-out or consent choices.
</p>

<h2>12. Children</h2>

<p>
  {appName} is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
  information from children under 13. If you believe a child has sent us personal information
  through support or another channel, contact us so we can review and delete it where appropriate.
</p>

<h2>13. Data Retention</h2>

<p>
  Local gameplay/settings data may remain on your device until you change it, reset it, delete the
  app, or clear the relevant local data through normal device or app behavior.
</p>

<p>
  Support emails may be kept for as long as reasonably needed to answer the request, maintain
  support records, resolve disputes, comply with legal obligations, or protect our rights.
</p>

<p>
  Google/AdMob, Apple, and other third-party providers retain data according to their own policies.
</p>

<h2>14. Security</h2>

<p>
  We use reasonable administrative and technical measures for the parts of {appName} and the
  OverLit website that we control. No app, website, network, device, or third-party service can be
  guaranteed to be perfectly secure. If you believe there is a privacy or security issue, contact us
  using the details below.
</p>

<h2>15. Privacy Rights</h2>

<p>
  Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access, correction, deletion,
  portability, restriction, objection, withdrawal of consent, or opt-out of certain sales, sharing,
  targeted advertising, or profiling. You may also have the right not to be discriminated against
  for exercising privacy rights.
</p>

<p>
  Because {appName} does not have accounts or a custom backend, many gameplay records are stored
  locally on your device. You can often control that local data by changing app settings, using
  in-app reset options where available, or deleting the app. For data handled by Google/AdMob,
  Apple, Meta/Instagram, TikTok, or other third parties, use their privacy tools and contact routes.
</p>

<p>
  To make a request about information we control directly, contact
  <code>{overLitConfig.supportEmail}</code>. We may need information to verify the request and may
  be unable to fulfill requests about data we do not control or cannot reasonably identify.
</p>

<h2>16. International Processing</h2>

<p>
  We are based in Poland. Third-party providers used for advertising, app distribution, platform
  services, support email, website hosting, or measurement may process information in other
  countries. Those countries may have privacy laws different from where you live.
</p>

<h2>17. Changes To This Policy</h2>

<p>
  We may update this policy as {appName} changes, including if advertising providers, consent
  flows, App Store disclosures, house ad behavior, or app features change. The effective date and
  version above show when this policy was last updated.
</p>

<h2>18. Contact</h2>

<p>For privacy questions or requests, contact:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Email: <code>{overLitConfig.supportEmail}</code></li>
  <li>Support page: <a href={supportPageUrl}>{supportPageUrl}</a></li>
  <li>Country: Poland</li>
</ul>
